%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: competency based model of TE
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: What is the primary focus of Competency-Based Teacher Education
      (CBTE)?
    Options:
    - The amount of time spent in coursework
    - The philosophical beliefs of the teacher
    - The demonstration of pre-specified, measurable competencies
    - The theoretical knowledge of educational psychology
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'In a CBTE program, a teacher''s progress is determined by:'
    Options:
    - Their ranking compared to peers
    - Their performance on a single final examination
    - The number of credit hours completed
    - Their demonstrated mastery of each competency
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a key characteristic of CBTE?
    Options:
    - Norm-referenced evaluation
    - Fixed time frame for all students
    - Criterion-referenced assessment
    - Emphasis on theoretical learning only
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The assessment in CBTE is best described as:'
    Options:
    - Subjective and holistic
    - Based on peer comparison
    - Objective and performance-based
    - Focused solely on written tests
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A major advantage of the CBTE model is its emphasis on:'
    Options:
    - Teacher autonomy and creativity
    - Accountability and measurable outcomes
    - Abstract theoretical knowledge
    - Unstructured learning experiences
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The statement "The teacher will be able to frame at least three
      different types of questions (factual, conceptual, analytical) in a 10-minute
      micro-teaching session" is an example of a:'
    Options:
    - Teaching philosophy
    - Lesson plan objective
    - Course description
    - Competency statement
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A significant criticism of the CBTE model is that it may lead
      to:'
    Options:
    - A lack of clear standards
    - The fragmentation of teaching into isolated skills
    - Overemphasis on theoretical understanding
    - Insufficient focus on practical skills
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The curriculum in a CBTE program is typically organized into:'
    Options:
    - Traditional semester-long courses
    - Large, interdisciplinary projects
    - Self-paced learning modules
    - Socratic dialogue sessions
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which model of teacher education is CBTE most closely related to?
    Options:
    - The Humanistic Model
    - The Behaviouristic Model
    - The Constructivist Model
    - The Romantic Model
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'In CBTE, the primary role of the teacher educator is that of a:'
    Options:
    - Philosopher and guide
    - Disciplinarian and authority
    - Co-learner and collaborator
    - Facilitator and assessor
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The concept of "mastery learning" in CBTE implies that:'
    Options:
    - All students will achieve the same rank.
    - A student progresses only after demonstrating proficiency in a competency.
    - Learning is a naturally unfolding process.
    - The fastest students are the most competent.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is the most appropriate assessment method
      for a CBTE program?
    Options:
    - A final essay on educational theory
    - A standardized multiple-choice test
    - An observation checklist of teaching skills during an internship
    - A subjective evaluation of teacher personality
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The development of a CBTE program begins with:'
    Options:
    - Selecting textbooks
    - Identifying essential teaching competencies
    - Designing lecture schedules
    - Planning field trips
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key difference between CBTE and traditional models is CBTE''s
      focus on:'
    Options:
    - Inputs (time, courses)
    - Outputs (demonstrable skills)
    - Philosophical foundations
    - Historical perspectives
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a potential "higher-order" competency
      that is difficult to assess in a pure CBTE framework?
    Options:
    - Writing a lesson plan
    - Using audio-visual equipment
    - Fostering a democratic classroom environment
    - Managing classroom transitions
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The CBTE model gained significant prominence during the:'
    Options:
    - 19th Century
    - 1920s
    - 2000s
    - 1970s
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'If a teacher candidate can re-take an assessment until they achieve
      mastery, this reflects the CBTE principle of:'
    Options:
    - Individualized pacing
    - Norm-referencing
    - Time-bound learning
    - Competitive evaluation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A "competency" in CBTE typically includes:'
    Options:
    - Only knowledge components
    - Only skill components
    - Knowledge, skills, and attitudes
    - Only attitudinal components
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The demerit of CBTE known as "reductionism" refers to its tendency
      to:'
    Options:
    - Increase the cost of teacher education
    - Reduce complex teaching to a list of simple skills
    - Lengthen the duration of teacher training
    - Overcomplicate the assessment process
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which regulatory body in India has incorporated competency-based
      approaches into its teacher education frameworks?
    Options:
    - UGC
    - NCERT
    - NCTE
    - AICTE
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher education program that uses a detailed "skills checklist"
      for final certification is most influenced by the:'
    Options:
    - Constructivist model
    - CBTE model
    - Humanistic model
    - Apprenticeship model
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The philosophical foundation of CBTE is most aligned with:'
    Options:
    - Existentialism
    - Idealism
    - Pragmatism and Empiricism
    - Perennialism
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'In a CBTE framework, feedback to teacher candidates is typically:'
    Options:
    - Vague and general
    - Delayed until the end of the program
    - Based on personal opinion
    - Immediate and specific to the competency
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is an example of a psychomotor competency
      for a teacher?
    Options:
    - Understanding child development
    - Believing in inclusive education
    - Skillfully using the chalkboard for diagramming
    - Appreciating poetry
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A major challenge in implementing CBTE is:'
    Options:
    - The lack of any clear standards
    - Defining and assessing complex, integrative competencies
    - Its complete reliance on theoretical exams
    - Its opposition to practical training
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The term "criterion-referenced" in CBTE means that assessment
      is based on:'
    Options:
    - How a candidate performs relative to others
    - A fixed percentage of students who must fail
    - A pre-established standard of performance
    - The subjective judgment of the evaluator
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'Micro-teaching is a strategy often used in CBTE because it:'
    Options:
    - Allows for the practice and assessment of specific teaching skills in isolation
    - Is a lengthy and comprehensive teaching exercise
    - Focuses solely on the teacher's content knowledge
    - Avoids the need for any feedback
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: CBTE can be seen as a response to the demand for greater _____
      in teacher education.
    Options:
    - Flexibility
    - Theoretical rigor
    - Public accountability
    - Philosophical depth
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a potential affective (attitudinal) competency?
    Options:
    - States the principles of inclusive education.
    - Demonstrates sensitivity towards students from diverse cultural backgrounds.
    - Designs a unit test with reliability.
    - Uses a video projector correctly.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teaching portfolio in a CBTE program is used to:'
    Options:
    - Replace all other forms of assessment
    - Showcase only the candidate's best work
    - Provide evidence of achievement across multiple competencies
    - Serve as a personal diary
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The CBTE model is most effective for ensuring that graduating
      teachers possess:'
    Options:
    - A unique and personal teaching style
    - A deep understanding of educational philosophy
    - A standardized set of basic teaching skills
    - A resistance to standardized curricula
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A critique of CBTE from a constructivist perspective is that it:'
    Options:
    - Is too student-centered
    - Undervalues the process of knowledge construction by the teacher
    - Lacks clear objectives
    - Is too focused on higher-order thinking
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The phrase "personalized instruction" in CBTE refers to:'
    Options:
    - Every candidate receiving the same instruction
    - Tailoring learning resources to help individuals achieve competencies
    - Allowing candidates to choose their own competencies
    - Eliminating the need for instructors
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a cognitive competency?
    Options:
    - Explains the causes of the Indian independence movement.
    - Maintains eye contact with students.
    - Shows patience when a student struggles.
    - Organizes the physical layout of the classroom.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ultimate goal of CBTE is to produce teachers who are:'
    Options:
    - Identical in their teaching methods
    - Effective performers of essential teaching tasks
    - Primarily theorists and researchers
    - Free to ignore standardized curricula
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'In a CBTE program, a candidate who fails a competency assessment
      is typically required to:'
    Options:
    - Drop out of the program
    - Repeat the entire academic year
    - Receive remedial help and reattempt the assessment
    - Accept a lower grade and move on
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The development of a "competency map" is a crucial step in designing
      a CBTE program. This map outlines:'
    Options:
    - The geographical location of practice teaching schools
    - The relationships and sequences between different competencies
    - The career paths for graduates
    - The budget for the program
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A potential negative consequence of CBTE is that it may encourage
      "teaching to the test," where the test is:'
    Options:
    - The final university examination
    - The competency checklist
    - The student satisfaction survey
    - The principal's evaluation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which teaching strategy is least aligned with the principles of
      CBTE?
    Options:
    - Simulation exercises
    - Programmed learning modules
    - Open-ended, student-directed inquiry projects
    - Micro-teaching sessions with feedback
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The CBTE model views teacher expertise as primarily consisting
      of:'
    Options:
    - Intuitive understanding
    - A repertoire of mastered competencies
    - Innate talent
    - Philosophical conviction
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'When assessing a competency like "classroom management," a CBTE
      assessor would look for:'
    Options:
    - The teacher's personal belief about discipline
    - Observable evidence of strategies to maintain a productive learning environment
    - The teacher's score on a personality test
    - Student scores on a standardized test
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The emphasis on "demonstration" in CBTE requires assessment to
      be:'
    Options:
    - Based solely on written statements
    - Subjective and narrative
    - Postponed until the end of the program
    - Conducted through authentic or simulated performance
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key difference between a "competency" and a "learning objective"
      is that a competency is:'
    Options:
    - More general and abstract
    - Focused specifically on the learner's demonstrable capability
    - Only concerned with knowledge
    - Not used for assessment purposes
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The legacy of CBTE is evident in contemporary trends such as:'
    Options:
    - Unstructured homeschooling
    - Standardized teaching standards and performance assessments (like edTPA)
    - The complete elimination of teacher certification
    - Sole reliance on apprentice-style training
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: A teacher education program that claims to be "outcomes-based"
      is most similar to a _____ program.
    Options:
    - CBTE
    - Traditional liberal arts
    - Philosophically-oriented
    - Subject-centered
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The term "performance-based" in PBTE (Performance-Based Teacher
      Education) highlights that assessment is based on:'
    Options:
    - The candidate's potential
    - The candidate's actual performance
    - The candidate's intentions
    - The candidate's theoretical knowledge
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A major contribution of the CBTE movement was to shift the question
      in teacher education from "What was taught?" to:'
    Options:
    - '"Who taught it?"'
    - '"How long did it take?"'
    - '"What was learned and can be demonstrated?"'
    - '"What is the teacher''s philosophy?"'
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'In a CBTE system, the transcript of a graduating teacher would
      primarily list:'
    Options:
    - Courses taken and grades received
    - Hours of field experience completed
    - Competencies mastered and the level of performance
    - Subjective comments from instructors
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a social competency for a teacher?
    Options:
    - Recites a poem with expression.
    - Collaborates effectively with colleagues and parents.
    - Solves a quadratic equation.
    - Defines the term 'learning disability'.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: competency based model of TE
